TITLE: Structural Radiative Element with Integrated Wide-Bandgap Semiconductor
Test Vehicle, Baked-In Deterministic Register Identity, and Blind Verification
by Pre-Committed Acceptance Bands

FIELD: Structural materials and semiconductor test engineering; specifically
elements whose thermal, structural, and sensing functions are integrated in a
single laminate, and methods for specifying, generating, and independently
verifying such elements deterministically.

BACKGROUND: (1) Heat-rejecting structures conventionally separate the radiator,
the structure, and the instrumentation into distinct systems joined by fluid
circuits. (2) Semiconductor devices are conventionally specified by datasheet
parameters verified against movable production tolerances. (3) Design documents
are conventionally regenerated non-deterministically, so a drawing cannot serve
as its own verification reference. A need exists for an element whose identity
is computed, not assigned; whose specification documents regenerate
byte-identically; and whose acceptance criteria are fixed and hash-committed
before any physical article exists.

SUMMARY: A laminate element comprises a radiating semiconductor skin layer
(e.g., silicon carbide), an insulating gradient layer disposed BEHIND the skin,
and a structural back layer. A wide-bandgap semiconductor test die is
integrated into the skin and reports the element's own temperature and leakage
electrically at operating temperatures (800-1,000 K class) at which silicon
devices are inoperative. Each element carries a register identity (E, Kd,
split, I) computed from its mass and mean density by a fixed form. A generator
issues the element's blueprint with the designer's identity embedded on the
face, in the file's metadata chunks, and in a companion sheet, and VERIFIES the
identity by read-back, refusing issuance on any failure. Regeneration of the
blueprint from the same inputs yields a byte-identical file (SHA-256 matched;
EQS-924). Acceptance bands for the die's electrical parameters are computed
from stated material classes and hash-committed BEFORE fabrication (EQS-919);
fabrication and measurement are performed by separated parties, and the
measuring party scores results against the committed bands without authority
to alter them (the blind discipline).

DETAILED DESCRIPTION - DETERMINISTIC REPLICATION (the encapsulated method):
(a) INPUT SET: an element is fully specified by (mass, mean density) and, for
the test die, by stated material-class inputs (drift thickness, doping,
critical field, mobility class, lifetime class).
(b) REGISTER COMPUTATION: E = E_earth + 1.5 ln(M/M_earth);
Kd = Kd_earth (rho_bar/rho_earth)^{1/2}; I = E - (1/2) ln Kd, with filed
constants. The computation is pure: identical inputs yield identical outputs
at full floating-point precision on re-execution (verified, EQS-924,
deviations 0.0).
(c) IDENTITY-GATED GENERATION: the blueprint generator embeds the designer
identity in three channels, reads all three back, and deletes partial output
and refuses issuance if any channel fails (EQS-901), including under a
deliberate tamper test.
(d) BYTE-IDENTICAL REGENERATION: re-generation from the input set reproduces
the blueprint image byte-for-byte (SHA-256 equality), making the document a
self-verifying artifact: any holder of the inputs can prove a presented
blueprint is the issued blueprint.
(e) PRE-COMMITTED ACCEPTANCE: before fabrication, expected electrical values
are computed from the class inputs (e.g., punch-through breakdown
Vbr = Ec*t - qNt^2/(2 eps_s)) and acceptance bands are fixed and recorded in
a payload-hashed record. A later measurement outside a band identifies and
invalidates the specific class input responsible (the kill rule); bands are
never revised after a measurement exists.
(f) BLIND VERIFICATION PROTOCOL: the fabricating party receives geometry
under confidentiality; the measuring party receives the article and the
committed bands' integrity hash, measures, and scores; neither party can
alter the bands or the register reference, both of which are independently
recomputable by any holder of the input set.

